# Git (truenas-config-backup)

This repo uses [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) so
[semantic-release](https://semantic-release.gitbook.io/) can bump on `main`. See
[CONTRIBUTING — Releasing](CONTRIBUTING.md#releasing) for release behavior.

**Agent commits:** always draft conventional subjects here — do not use plain imperative
subjects, even though this repo is under `~/Documents/personal_repos/`.

- Subject: `type: description`, `type(scope): description`, or `type!: description`
- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `perf`, `revert`, `chore`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `test`, `build`, `ci`
- No trailing period on the subject
- Optional short body focusing on **why**
- No Jira IDs
- Only commit when explicitly requested; never push unless asked

Examples: `feat: add backup retention policy`, `fix(auth): reject empty dashboard password`,
`docs: update README install steps`

**Local enforcement:** global hooks at `~/.config/git/hooks` skip conventional checks when the
branch has no Jira ID. For strict local validation (like
[plextraktbox](https://github.com/CampAsAChamp/plextraktbox)), use repo-local
`.githooks/commit-msg` and `git config core.hooksPath .githooks`.
